<title>HUNGARY: CEFTA 1996 AUTO SALES -- TABLE.</title>
<headline>CEFTA 1996 AUTO SALES -- TABLE.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>New auto sales in Central</p>
<p>European Free Trade Agreement (CEFTA) countries rose 39.5</p>
<p>percent to 842,565 units in 1996 from 603,780 units in 1995,</p>
<p>according to a Reuters survey.</p>
<p>CEFTA, which was formed in 1993, includes the Czech</p>
<p>Republic, Hungary, Poland, Slovakia and Slovenia. The survey,</p>
<p>which Reuters issues monthly, defines autos as cars, minibuses,</p>
<p>pickups, vans and other four-wheeled motor vehicles not over</p>
<p>5.0 tonnes in gross weight.</p>
